Integration: SDD

Purpose:
  Integration testing — verify multiple components work together correctly.
  Integration tests sit between unit tests and E2E tests in the pyramid.

Owns: ./

Scope:
  Multiple components interacting
  API endpoints with database
  Service-to-service communication
  Message queue interactions
  External dependency integration

Principles:
  Test real interactions, not mocks (where possible)
  Use test containers for databases
  Clean state between tests
  Test both success and failure paths
  Verify contracts between components

Structure:
  Every integration test MUST:
    involve at least two components
    test the interaction, not individual components
    use realistic data and configurations
    clean up all created resources

Frameworks:
  Go: testcontainers, httptest
  Laravel: PHPUnit + HTTP tests, Orchestra Testbench
  Node: Jest + supertest, testcontainers
  General: Docker Compose, Testcontainers

Navigation:
  Project: @project/project.sdd
  Workflow: @workflow/testing.sdd
  TestLevels: @levels.sdd
  TestTypes: @types.sdd
  TestGates: @gates.sdd
  BDD: @bdd.sdd
  Unit: @unit.sdd
  API: @api.sdd
  Contract: @contract.sdd
  ProjectTesting: @instances/vkard.az/testing/INDEX.sdd

